  "worked_solution": "First, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(m+1)! & =(m+1)\\cdot m! \\\\ m! & =m\\cdot (m-1)!\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can cancel the $m!$ and $(m-1)!$ that occur in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(m!)^{2}}{(m+1)!\\,(m-1)!} & =\\frac{m!\\cdot m!}{(m+1)!\\,(m-1)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{m!\\cdot m\\cdot (m-1)!}{(m+1)\\cdot m!\\cdot (m-1)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{m!}\\cdot m\\cdot \\cancel{(m-1)!}}{(m+1)\\cdot \\cancel{m!}\\cdot \\cancel{(m-1)!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{m}{m+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
